<section style="padding:0 0 110px"><div class="narrow" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);justify-items:center"><img src="/images/founder.png" alt="Abhijeet, founder of Funnele" style="width:100%;max-width:460px;height:auto;display:block"></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 0 120px"><div class="narrow">
  <p class="p" style="font-size:19px;margin:0 0 22px">Most store owners buy SEO and web development from two different people. One builds a site that Google struggles to read. The other brings in visitors who leave a site that doesn't sell. We work on both, in one plan.</p>
  <p class="p" style="font-size:19px;margin:0 0 22px">SEO and website development share one goal: a fast, clear site that answers buyers' questions. That is what search rewards, and it is also what sells. We fix the foundations first, then grow from there.</p>
  <p class="p" style="font-size:19px;margin:0">We take on a small number of stores at a time, so the people who plan the work are the people who deliver it and report on it.</p>
</div></section>
<section style="padding:0 0 130px"><div class="wrap g2">
  <div style="border-top:2px solid var(--red);padding-top:26px"><h3 class="disp" style="font-size:30px;margin:0 0 14px">Search and website, together</h3><p class="p" style="font-size:16px">Your SEO and your website are planned as one project, so nothing gets fixed twice or left half-done between teams.</p></div>
  <div style="border-top:2px solid var(--red);padding-top:26px"><h3 class="disp" style="font-size:30px;margin:0 0 14px">Built to be found and to sell</h3><p class="p" style="font-size:16px">Every page we build or improve has a search job and a buying job. We measure both, and report on both every month.</p></div>
</div></section>

